{"title":"Career roadmap · Quality Controller — Textile","role":"Quality Controller — Textile","summary":"A Textile Quality Controller is responsible for ensuring that fibres, yarns, fabrics, garments and finished textile products meet defined specifications for strength, appearance, dimensional stability, colour, construction, performance, safety and customer requirements.","facts":{"Starts":"Year 1 UG · 2026","Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Textile Engineering / Technology","Timeline assumption":"4-year engineering degree beginning in 2026, with graduation around 2030."},"about":[{"label":"Primary skills","text":"Textile testing, quality inspection, statistical quality control, defect analysis, process control"},{"label":"Additional skills","text":"ISO systems, Lean Six Sigma, SPC, Excel, Power BI, ERP/MES and automation"}],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Textile Quality Intern, Lab Intern, Quality Trainee, Production/QA Intern"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Quality Engineer, Quality Controller, QA Executive, Textile Testing Engineer"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Quality Engineer, Quality Specialist, Process Quality Engineer"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Quality Manager, QA Manager, Technical Quality Manager, Head of Quality"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Tech/B.E. Textile Engineering / Technology graduate, this is a direct career pathway. The student should combine textile science with quality-management systems, testing, statistics, root-cause analysis, laboratory practices, production knowledge and increasingly digital quality analytics."},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Tech Textile Engineering","Quality/Lab Internship","Quality Engineer / Quality Executive","Textile Quality Controller","Senior Quality Engineer 